{"kind":"report","text":"Changes requested: R5 slice B (items 6 and 7, failure bounds and authenticated control cleanup) at exact head 2d8039a32cc1648cf5efeebeeeba567cc08e7948, tree 43c4bd7e4697acea616254a1e291c28c15cb2f34 (review request f61b9649, promise 2b9ce62f, implementation 81de9c9b / 216a9ac4). There is one required documentation finding, F1, of the same class as F1 in my slice A review 982a82b1. I found no code defect. The code, witnesses, controls and gate pass my checks. A successor that changes only the sentence in F1 needs no new gate (docs/testing.md:597), and its review is short.\n\nRead order: I read the primary, notes/implementation/2026-10-24-hosted-mcp-failure-cleanup.md (artifact 2e499d39), first and in full. Then I read the whole diff from the branch base f13e261b: hosted.ts, the two test files, docs/mcp.md and the seal. For the ordering claims I read HostedAgent.#control_, #expire and #authorized, and HostedRegistry.create, at the head. The branch starts at e124c676, merges the slice A Main (5cdf49bf) and the capacity deferral head (bb7d531c), records the gate at f230ff2 (tree 6d5278d9) and adds only the note at 2d8039a3 (22 insertions, 1 deletion). Its merge-base with Main 920c9051 is f13e261b, and merging the head into Main gives exactly its tree, 43c4bd7e. The diff from f13e261b touches six paths, and the act log holds a pointer at this head for each of them.\n\nF1 (required, documentation). docs/mcp.md:1777-1778 says the bounded failure window and authenticated cleanup \"are recorded in the failure-cleanup note; validation and deployment of that follow-up are pending.\" Validation has closed: gate 5924 passed at f230ff2, and the note records it. Once this head lands, the sentence is false on Main. Requested fix: say that the note records the implementation and its validation, including the passing gate, and that deployment is pending. Nothing else in the document, the note or the code needs to change.\n\nRequest 81de9c9b's conditions, checked in the source:\n- Finite failure storage, no eviction of active entries. BearerFailures keeps at most 4,096 address keys, each at most 64 UTF-8 bytes with at most ten timestamps: a key at ten recent failures is refused before another timestamp is pushed, and a new key is added only when the map holds fewer than 4,096 keys after pruning keys whose every timestamp has expired. An oversized address is refused before authentication and is never truncated or hashed. A valid bearer on a new address authenticates even at capacity, because the capacity check comes after authenticate(). Success still clears no failures. The address is cf-connecting-ip, as before.\n- Authenticated cleanup ordering. In #control_ the expiry write moved from before #row() into the committing transaction, after the binding (bound), membership, signature and authority checks. A denied control reads the agent row and returns a fixed body; it writes nothing. The budget reserve that answers 507 runs inside the same transaction after #expire, so an authorized control still frees expired answer bytes before its budget is checked; no liveness is lost by the move. HostedRegistry.create already checks binding, link, membership and authority before its reservation transaction, whose first statement is the expiry; it is unchanged, and the agent's own create runs only after that registry check.\n- Preserved: the bearer protocol, replay (same op and fingerprint returns the retained answer), retention (seven days past notAfter) and accounting (cleanup credits exactly the expired answer bytes, once). Slice A admission is untouched: hosted-tools.ts, service.ts and catalogue.ts keep their seals.\n- No setting, no deployment, no bearer expiry or plaintext migration. The note says so, and the diff has none.\n\nWitnesses. hosted-failures.test.ts (two Node cases) fills 4,096 keys, shows three new failing addresses refused without eviction while a limited address never reaches authenticate(), a valid bearer accepted at capacity, one expired slot admitting one new address while the others stay active, ten-per-minute with success clearing nothing, the 64-byte boundary with 32 two-byte characters admitted and 33 refused, and null and \"\" sharing one bucket. hosted.scope.test.ts (the H2 to H4 case) snapshots the agent's control rows, agent row, sessions, budget, counts and durable facts and the registry's control rows, agents and budget, sends a bearer control and a create signed with the wrong key for the named actor, gets 403 signature from each, and asserts both snapshots unchanged; then the authorized stale replay performs the cleanup, crediting exactly the answer bytes, and a second replay credits nothing twice. The runs are the real Worker routes on the real objects.\n\nControls, each on hosted.ts bytes with SHA-256 496bdf46, equal to the head's, with the file restored to that digest:\n- capacity (control-capacity-evidence v1): removing the capacity refusal fails \"new failures cannot evict an active window: expected 'unauthorized' to be 'limited'\" (1 failed, 1 passed). The wrapper's own classifier rejected the run for an unrelated stack frame; the raw vitest result is the named red, and the wrapper verdict is kept as recorded.\n- address (control-address-evidence v2): removing the byte bound fails \"an overlong address reached bearer authentication\" (1 failed, 1 passed). The v1 attempt stopped at a preflight check before any mutation, as the note says.\n- cleanup (control-cleanup-evidence v1): moving the expiry write back before authentication fails \"invalid signature changes no answer, budget, session or agent state\" (1 failed, 16 passed).\n\nGate 5924, raw folder /private/tmp/artroom-security-r5b-gate-evidence-20261024-v1, reviewed from the closed manifest at /private/tmp/artroom-security-r5b-gate-independent-review-evidence-20261024-v1/manifest.json (SHA-256 66766047; all 8 payloads and all 42 pinned raw inputs match their digests): result.json records expectedHead f230ff2, expectedTree 6d5278d9, unchangedCheckpoint true, gatePassed true, child exit 0; before.json and after.json are byte-identical with a clean status. stdout.log shows all eight stages exit 0. stages/test.log reads \"Test Files 496 passed | 1 skipped (497)\" and \"Tests 3531 passed | 3 skipped (3534)\"; the Node block reports pass 39 fail 0 and the Counting block pass 55 fail 0. The two new Node cases pass at lines 2389-2390 and the H2 to H4 case at line 2909. The head differs from f230ff2 only in the note, so docs/testing.md:597 needs no rerun. The compiler failure 24262, the wrapper rejection 59118 and the preflight failure 91824 stay recorded as failures. The callback gaps (13 ready, 31 result) are a reporting limitation; every terminal record passed, and the 19 affected cases have complete callbacks.\n\nDocument checks at 2d8039a3:\n- git diff --check from f13e261b is clean;\n- check-commit-messages from f13e261b reports 9 checked, 0 flagged; the longest new subject is 63 characters;\n- section citations on an export report 1,877 resolved, 0 broken and 5 known unresolved; the citation script is identical to Main's;\n- merging the head into Main 920c9051 gives exactly its tree, 43c4bd7e.\n\nArchitecture: the failure window becomes one small class with one method and three constants, and the agent calls it with the authentication as a closure, so the order of bound, throttle, authentication and capacity is read in one place. The cleanup moves into the transaction that already decides replay, budget and the action, so a control either commits everything or writes nothing.\nSecurity: I found no defect. Memory per agent is bounded by construction: 4,096 keys of at most 64 bytes with at most ten timestamps each. An attacker who fills the map from many addresses can make failed requests from further new addresses answer 429 instead of 401 for a minute, and can never evict an active throttle or stop a valid bearer. A denied control can no longer cause a write, which closes the agent half of item 7 (6dd06d03 section 1.5). The hosted.ts seal changes to the maintained parser's value, and the entry-point Node block passed in the gate on identical bytes. The address is the edge-set cf-connecting-ip; where that header could be forged, the per-address throttle was already weak, and that is unchanged by this head.\nSimplification: about 60 lines changed in hosted.ts and no shim. Nonblocking: key.length \u003e 64 is implied by utf8(key).length \u003e 64 and could go; the pruning loop at capacity visits all 4,096 keys on each refused new address, which is cheap and only reached under attack.\n\nResidual risk for the planner's deploy, unchanged from slice A: a deploy from Main closes hosted MCP on a Worker unless MCP_ENABLED is set there; decision 10f45efc keeps it closed. This head adds no setting.\n\nFor approval of the successor I need a tree that differs from 2d8039a3 only in the F1 sentence. Nothing else here needs to be redone. No deployment or hosted claim is made or approved here.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:2e499d39a5f57f2d16bac5e1a50202e22a1e8214","binding":"assigned","head":"2d8039a32cc1648cf5efeebeeeba567cc08e7948","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:2b9ce62fa705f8458b89faa2db549a7b294416b0\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:216a9ac405978f27f37b16c8dbfbcdbdd1b7c3e2\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:65c7e1cbc77bb61012fd231f6df8504f95d93479","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"changes-requested"}}